+- **Every operator of Def. 11.8 is built; each is generated only where its premise was OBSERVED.** The
+  catalog's seven partial or unsupported operators (the dict key/value swap, ctype to and from a set,
+  field, class, clamp, raise-inject, state-extra) each needed a fact about a function's VALUES that a
+  type name cannot give. `Wesker.codomain.observe_codomain` runs the tests once against the original and
+  records every return (its line and value), every exception that left the function and each argument's
+  state before and after each call; a premised operator is generated at a return site only where the
+  perturbation was APPLIED to every value the site returned and did not raise, so it never raises on an
+  observed value and a value the baseline never saw comes back unchanged. The result is a
+  `frozenset[str]`, the type Detective's cache already carries. 36 built, 2 realized by another operator
+  (0, and state-noop by the positive `STATE:remove_assign` and `STMT`, decision D2), none partial or
+  unsupported. (W#44; Detective #120–#123)
+  - `dict`: the swap, where every observed dict has hashable values. `ctype`: list or tuple to a set where
+    the observed elements are hashable; set to a sorted list and frozenset to a sorted tuple where they are
+    mutually orderable (a deterministic order, not iteration order).
+  - `field`, one field at a time on a dataclass, namedtuple, attrs class or plain object, the field names
+    and types taken from the observed instances: a field to its type's default, moved a step, or exchanged
+    with the previous field of its type. `class`: a copy rebound to a dynamically created subclass (what
+    separates `type(x) is C` from `isinstance`) and, where there is one, to its user base.
+  - `clamp`: into the observed range narrowed by one step on each side, so a value at an edge changes.
+  - `raise`: injects the exception types the function is observed to raise (else those its own body
+    raises) at the return point. An injected raise fails every test that reaches the call, so it is
+    `reach_class` (`kill_class_of_dimension`), not a pin of the output. `state-extra`: one extra write to a
+    mutable argument or receiver the baseline observed never mutated.
+  - A premise that was measured and failed is named per function, with the exception the attempt raised, in
+    the profile's `mu_minus_withheld`; an operator whose premise the function never offers is named there too.
+- **Typing is by return SITE.** `tag(n)` returns a str on one branch and None on the other; a test that
+  reaches only the first observed `{str}` for the function, and the `return None` no test ran got four str
+  rewrites that raise on None. Each return statement now answers for the values it returned
+  (`site_mode_standing`); an unexecuted one gets only the always-applicable modes, and an incomplete
+  observation (a test was cut) licenses nothing else. A type-name-only observation still types the function
+  as a whole. (W#44, AC2)
+- **`run_function_profiling(..., two_sign=True)`** adds OUTPUT to the categories and observes the codomain
+  when the caller supplied none. **`MutationPolicy.unbuilt`** is a field (None for the one-sign policy,
+  `{}` for the two-sign one) instead of only a hashed value. (W#44, AC1)
+
 The one-sign universe and its id are unchanged by this. Two-sign id `9+neg.aaff90df3dbf` →
 `9+neg.8144c37b1638`, and the two-sign fingerprint's OUTPUT column rises on every corpus function.
