+## Premised operators
+
+A premised operator (Def. 11.10) applies only where a fact about the observed VALUES guarantees it. The
+fact is established by APPLYING the perturbation to every value the site returned
+(`Wesker.mu_minus.apply_value_mode`): the mode is generated at the site only if no application raised
+and at least one changed its value. A failed application is recorded with the exception's type, so the
+function's profile says which premise failed. The premise is therefore the guarantee that the operator
+never raises on an observed value, and a value the baseline never saw comes back unchanged from the
+mutant (`perturb_return`), never as a crash kill.
+
+| sub-mode | premise |
+|---|---|
+| `return_swap_items` | every dict returned at the site has hashable values |
+| `return_to_set` | every list or tuple returned at the site has hashable elements |
+| `return_from_set` | every set or frozenset returned at the site has mutually orderable elements |
+| `return_field_drop` | every value returned at the site is a record with that field, of a type that has a default |
+| `return_field_bump` | every value returned at the site is a record with that field, of a numeric, boolean, str or bytes type |
+| `return_field_swap` | every value returned at the site is a record with both fields, of one type |
+| `return_class_subclass` | every value returned at the site is an instance of a Python-defined class that can be copied and rebound to a subclass |
+| `return_class_base` | every value returned at the site is an instance of a class with a user base class, copied and rebound to it |
+| `return_clamp` | every value returned at the site is one finite, mutually ordered kind (int and float, Decimal, date, naive datetime, timedelta) with at least two distinct values |
+
+A parameterized mode carries its parameter after `@`: the field (`return_field_drop@x`), the pair
+(`return_field_swap@x,y`), the narrowed bounds (`return_clamp@i5,i9`). The two parameterized Form B
+modes are `raise_inject@<exception path>` and `state_extra@<parameter>`; their premises are in the
